<p>Vermouth is an aromatic fortified wine that’s flavoured with various botanicals and is sometimes coloured.</p>
<p>Traditionally, Vermouth was used for medicinal purposes (we’ve heard that one before, am I right guys?) but was later served as an aperitif in fashionable Turin cafes in the mid to late 18th century.</p>
<p>By the 19th century, it’d become popular with bartenders in the creation of fancy cocktails such as the <a href="/cocktails/dry-martini/">Martini</a>, the <a href="/cocktails/manhattan/">Manhattan</a> and the <a href="/cocktails/rob-roy/">Rob Roy</a>, and later the <a href="/cocktails/negroni/">Negroni</a>.</p>
